{"seq":11,"trial_id":"gbrain-memory-2026-10/qm-pi-sonnet-gbrain-told-live-mu-memory/ms-06-phl-tickets/r2","wall_ts":"2026-10-26T22:35:08.884Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"4ca2972a4c0db8913578c014a0424d212dce3531402a3441f297a565b9a8751f","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","text":"Bettina, here is the list for Kwame's review. Nothing in #coastal-team or #coastal-random mentions a ticket or feature request for either account. Everything below comes from Moss's Coastal cheat sheet and a note of yours.\n\n**Pellucid Harbor Logistics (PHL, Gulf Coast)**\n- **Ticket #4419** (open): the `Yard_Dwell_Summary` report times out when filtered by container length. Source: Moss's cheat sheet.\n- **Ticket #PD-8841**: chassis pool holds on double-booked gates, Gate 4B, raised by the night dispatcher Hector. Source: your cutover recap note from 2025-12-08. That note doesn't say whether it is still open.\n\n**Driftmoor Marine Freight (DMF, Puget Sound)**\n- **Feature request #882**: a bulk-clear button for departed barges, requested by their warehouse managers. Source: Moss's cheat sheet.\n- **Tide-table import macro failure on Terminal B**: engineering supplied a manual CSV patch for the night dispatcher. The cheat sheet gives no ticket number, so I haven't assigned one.\n\n**Left out**\n- **Pellow Home Living / Covey & Lark Retail:** I excluded it, including ticket #8812 (the Door 4B scanner fix).\n- **Saltmarsh Provisions:** I excluded it, including ticket PD-4827 (the admin access issue).\n\nI only found Moss's cheat sheet and your recap note. If Moss keeps other Coastal notes that I can't see, anything in them is missing from this list."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","ts":"1791986400.000124"}}
